  "title": "Kirby Problem 1.26",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(Jones Slope Conjecture). For a knot $K$, the Jones slopes $js(K)$\nare the set of cluster points in\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\frac{4}{n^{2}}\\deg_{+}\\bigl(J_{n}(K;q)\\bigr)\\right\\}_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}}\n\\cup\n\\left\\{\\frac{4}{n^{2}}\\deg_{-}\\bigl(J_{n}(K;q)\\bigr)\\right\\}_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}},\n$$\n\nwhere deg $^{+}$ denotes the highest degree and deg $^{-}$ the lowest degree.",
